MetaMask Brand Impersonation – No User Interaction

Severity: Low
Status: Confirmed Phishing – No User Engagement
Category: Brand Impersonation / Credential Harvesting Attempt

1. Executive Summary

On June 4–5, 2025, a phishing email impersonating MetaMask was delivered to inquiry@mydfir.com. The message claimed an “Unrecognized Login Attempt” in order to create urgency and prompt user action.

Header analysis revealed spoofed infrastructure, homoglyph obfuscation, and PHP mailer artifacts consistent with phishing kit deployment. Telemetry review confirmed no user interaction occurred, and no compromise was observed.

