4. Technical Analysis
Email Origin

The message did not originate from legitimate MetaMask infrastructure. Instead:

Sent via PHP mailer from shared hosting

Used randomized sender address

Employed homoglyph and domain impersonation techniques

Relied on urgency-based social engineering

These characteristics indicate phishing kit automation rather than targeted enterprise compromise.

5. User Interaction Analysis

Multiple telemetry sources were reviewed:

EmailEvents

No open, preview, delete, or report actions recorded.

UrlClickEvents

No link click activity detected during relevant timeframe.

EmailPostDeliveryEvents

No post-delivery actions logged.

Conclusion: No user interaction occurred.

No credential submission, no endpoint execution, and no suspicious authentication events were observed.

